speechtext:
Madam Speaker, I rise under Standing Order 43 on a matter of urgent and pressing necessity.
Whereas the Minister of Agriculture has consistently described Canada's beef marketing system as "archaic" and "medieval"; whereas beef producers are busy attempting to produce beef under difficult and trying conditions and have neither the time nor the resources available to research and recommend changes to the system; and whereas the minister has marketing experts on staff and the resources of his department to assist him, 1 therefore move, seconded by the hon. member for Prince Albert (Mr. Hovdebo);
That this House instruct the minister to prepare and table a proposal outlining his ideas on an up-to-date beef marketing system.
